    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2SnxWxFd1BzigKY2tZa4GJe)_\n\nA query table can now be sorted by several columns, applied in the order they are set.\n\n**How I read the request:** \"sort a column based on multiple parameters, set in order\" as a primary sort key plus tie-breakers (like a spreadsheet's multi-level sort), each with its own direction.\n\n- `:sort-by` may be a list of columns: the first is the primary key, each next one breaks ties of those before it. An element may be `(COLUMN . asc)` or `(COLUMN . desc)`; plain columns use `:sort-desc`. A single column still works.\n- The sort is stable, so ties keep the query order (before, descending reversed them too).\n- Menu: `o` reads the columns in order (`rating,title:desc`); `O` is the default direction for columns without their own.\n- vui: clicking a column makes it primary and keeps the earlier clicks as tie-breakers (the number after the arrow is the rank); a Reset button returns to the spec's sort.\n- exc and Org renderers, the dynamic block and saved views take the list through the spec; the summary line says \"sorted by ...\". exc's own in-grid sorting is not touched.\n- New `tests/sp-collection-query-tables-test.el` (core sort with stubbed Vulpea, passes on Emacs 29.3). Menu and vui were not run in Emacs.\n- Literate doc and CHANGELOG updated. Based on main after #169.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCVTBv7t5Co86gQ2fN)_",
